    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="96fe625d-f5d9-57f0-a83b-7d0d57a4b405" activityNameId="f7ffb8b0-445c-5549-a936-0dc5a385518b" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Cantilever retaining wall, construction, reinforced concrete</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Cantilever retaining wall, construction, reinforced concrete
Modern Swiss und European technologies are applied to building machines, material production and building processes. 
UUID: 65adcf54-89cb-474c-94dd-2350c86383b6
This process models 1 meter cantilever retaining wall with a height of 5.4 meters. Production phase (A1–A3) and construction phase/ transport (A4–A5) for 1 meter of installed cantiliever retaining wall, as well as trench excavation, foundation and backfilling are included. Disposal and deconstruction processes are excluded and modelled separately. Service life time 50 years
Location: Switzerland
Technology: According to ASTRA (2025), project specific data related to study "Anwendung der Ökobilanz-Methode für die Infrastruktur von Nationalstrassen".
Time period: Review of data currency scheduled after 5 years.
Production volume: 
Sampling: 
Extrapolations: None
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_65adcf54-89cb-474c-94dd-2350c86383b6.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
